{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc 'cat research_journal.md method_notes.json method.py solve.sh'","aggregated_output":"# Forecasting research journal\n\n## Current best\nUpdated 2026-10-06, resumed at 13:08 UTC. Retained best is the **unheaded, cross-fitted conditional tree/network gate** in `method.py`, complete masked MAE **14.018026311821254**, normalized score **2.9658123722093266**, evaluation `91f2c8e6729a47cd8ec7dfff72700664`. This improves the turn-start horizon-scheduled blend **14.030202610462462** by **0.012176298641208**. Both later structural extensions were reverted based on their actual protected results. Final verification is running.\n\nEvery public number below is an actual `./solve.sh` response using unchanged seeds **17, 29, 43**, fresh fits and independent checkpoint reloads. Successful runs passed shape, finiteness and reload gates. Lower complete masked MAE wins. Only public calibration targets and public features were accessed; no development labels, held-out/reference data, other track, target reconstruction from cross-sample histories, downloads or scorer edits. `solve.sh`, task files and frozen public assets are unchanged (SHA-256 checks passed). Fits/predictions use at most two CPU threads. Submission has 16 Python files, within source and state limits.\n\n## Runnable method\n`method.py` calls `conditional_calibration.py`. Fit a pooled median residual tree and specialists for horizons 1-6 / 7-12, blending pooled/specialist corrections equally. Trees: 90 stages, 15 leaves, leaf minimum 250, L2 20. Inputs contain base/anchor/history summaries, forecast slopes, clock/horizon, sensor identity, and eight sensor neighbors learned from correlations of within-history changes, with scale-normalized context.\n\nA NumPy residual network uses six-dimensional sensor embeddings, 48/24 tanh layers, a linear skip, two daily Fourier harmonics, smooth absolute loss (2 traffic units), and 100 Adam epochs/batch 4096. Three contiguous calibration-origin cross-fits supply held-out tree/network forecasts to a seven-variable sigmoid gate. Gate inputs: horizon, relative anchor/base and recent/base disagreement, history variability, expert disagreement and flow level. Fit smooth MAE with coefficient penalty 0.01 toward the 0.18 short / 0.32 long network schedule; clip prediction weight to [0.05, 0.65]. The retained network uses the original summary inputs. Sensor-seasonal heads, chronological/relative-history inputs and parameter averaging remain implemented as experimental options, with their protected/local outcomes below.\n\nCalibration has 74 hourly origins, 12 horizons and 170 sensors, about three days. Local validation consistently uses seed 17: train 0:50/test 50:74 (last) and train 0:25 plus 49:74/test 25:49 (middle). Inner cross-fits never train on their validation origins. Local MAE is diagnostic, not the protected result.\n\n## This turn: complete public evaluations\n| Method | Complete masked MAE | Decision / evaluation ID |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| Unchanged horizon-scheduled blend | 14.030202610462462 | Exactly reproduced prior best; `6f0e278479c440a59fef7b5ef6c8d1cb` |\n| Learned conditional gate | 14.018026311821254 | Retained; score 2.9658123722; `91f2c8e6729a47cd8ec7dfff72700664` |\n| Gate + summary/relative-history network ensemble | 14.031298204247088 | Rejected, restored gate; `ecd8bde9d5b04e279793e583ef181784` |\n| Matching gate + sensor-seasonal summary-network head | 14.020179462432948 | Rejected; score 2.9612635046; `a06af989351344a586996d35fbbc0abd` |\nFinal verification of the restored best is pending; record its actual response before ending the turn.\n\n## This turn: implemented structural experiments\nValues are last / middle local masked MAE under the paired splits above.\n\n- **Conditional gate:** old blend 13.4495945 / 13.1982899. Gate penalty 0.04 gave 13.4498315 / 13.2018042; 0.01 gave **13.4485098 / 13.1962305**; 0.002 gave 13.4520833 / 13.1820429. Selected 0.01 for improvement on both blocks; complete protected gain **0.0121762986**.\n- **Chronological network inputs:** expose all 12 history deviations from recent average plus first/last forecast-shape coordinates. Replacement 13.5318871 / 13.2745685; summary/history ensemble 13.4684167 / 13.2077393. Rejected. Adding sensor history scale, relative flow and relative anchor/recent disagreement: replacement 13.4916316 / 13.2140823; summary/relative-history ensemble 13.4489485 / 13.1751569. Applying the retained gate to this ensemble gave **13.4455352 / 13.1797128**, but protected MAE regressed, so rejected. Calibration-fit MAE fell from summary 12.1484 / 12.1125 to relative-history 11.8673 / 11.8145 while pure validation worsened: overfitting/variance is a plausible cause.\n- **Regularized sensor-seasonal head:** six jointly optimized coefficients per sensor: intercept, normalized horizon, daily and twice-daily sine/cosine; L2 0.0005. With old gate, headed final-iterate replacement 13.4227227 / 13.1800403. After recomputing matching inner OOF headed networks and fitting the gate: **13.4311238 / 13.1772847**, versus unheaded gate 13.4485098 / 13.1962305. Selected for complete scoring.\n- **Parameter averaging:** average network/embedding/head parameters from epochs 75-99. Matching headed gate 13.4457018 / 13.1733489, worse paired mean than final iterate. Relative-history auxiliary averaging also worsened its final-iterate ensemble (13.4462919 / 13.1809799 versus 13.4455352 / 13.1797128). Rejected; implementation remains optional in `neural_calibration.py`.\n\nFeature-only distribution check: development anchor/base relative disagreement has a heavier extreme tail (99th percentile 1.492 versus calibration 0.583), despite similar flow/history variability. Gate inputs/weights are capped. Local improvements can fail to transfer, as the richer-network ensemble demonstrated.\n\n## Earlier research retained for continuity\n| Earlier complete public method | Masked MAE | Decision |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| Initial identity | 15.4218571566 | Original baseline |\n| Robust pooled + sensor linear residuals | 15.0648913575 | Superseded |\n| Median residual tree, 90 stages | 14.1452638897 | Superseded; repeated runs reproduced exactly |\n| Tree, 180 stages | 14.1455193190 | Rejected |\n| Learned sensor-neighborhood tree | 14.1214289791 | Superseded |\n| Neighbor tree + robust sensor affine correction | 14.1433545829 | Rejected despite local gains |\n| Anchor-aligned seasonal innovations | 14.1209047365 | Superseded |\n| Partially pooled horizon specialists | 14.1101708074 | Superseded |\n| Trees + constant 25% smooth network | 14.0354537227 | Superseded |\n| Quarter-strength cross-fitted neural correction | 14.0429518732 | Rejected despite local gains |\n| Horizon-scheduled 18%/32% smooth network | 14.0302026105 | Superseded by gate |\n\nEarlier local-only failures: explicit history lags/sensor profiles in trees, robust summaries, heteroscedastic residual scaling, neighbor seasonal innovations, three horizon groups, Poisson origin-bootstrap trees, physical-graph replacement/augmentation and initial short-training network. Two horizon groups with partial pooling and the summary/Fourier/linear-skip network were useful. Supporting implementations remain available; do not repeat these unchanged experiments.\n\n## Next discriminating experiment\nTest graph sharing of only the four periodic sensor-head coefficients, using the history-derived neighborhood and a smoothness penalty; keep sensor intercept/horizon independent and use an intercept/horizon-only head as the control. Independent seasonal heads improved both local blocks but slightly worsened protected MAE, so this experiment should distinguish seasonal overfitting from a useful shared seasonal correction. Extend the existing network module (already 16 Python files), compare the same two origin blocks with matching OOF gates, then run the unchanged complete seed protocol only for a promising structural candidate; retain the current unheaded gate unless protected MAE decreases.\n\n## Resume 2026-10-06 13:39 UTC (in progress)\nRead the task contract and this journal. The unchanged method was submitted first through `./solve.sh`, but the public client returned HTTP 409. A single diagnostic retry of the same public client exposed the response: `{\"status\": \"busy\", \"message\": \"Your own evaluation is already running\"}`. No new metric was returned; this appears to be the preceding final verification still occupying the scorer. The prior best remains unchanged in `method.py`.\nImplemented optional sensor heads: (a) intercept/horizon only; (b) full seasonal head with a symmetric learned-neighborhood Laplacian penalty applied only to the four Fourier coefficients. Baseline defaults are unchanged. Running paired public-calibration origin-block validation before choosing a candidate for complete protected scoring.\n\nUnchanged public baseline retry completed successfully: MAE **14.018026311821254**, score **2.9658123722093266**, evaluation `d57fa2ee96f14f6998a523259deea07a`, seeds 17/29/43 and all quality gates passed. This exactly reproduces the retained best. Paired local baseline MAE is 13.4485102 / 13.1962309 (float rounding agrees with the earlier journal). Implemented an additional optional agreement gate using expert distance advantages relative to anchor, recent average and last observation; it is inactive in the baseline and will be assessed using matching OOF forecasts.\n\nSensor-head local results (last / middle, seed 17): trend-only head with retained gate **13.4403821 / 13.1884937**; graph-seasonal head with retained gate **13.4256359 / 13.1796024**. Recomputing matching inner OOF experts/gates gives trend **13.4464581 / 13.1907885**, graph **13.4326290 / 13.1833977**. Both improve both baseline blocks; graph is stronger. Graph penalty is 0.005 times the symmetric learned-neighbor Laplacian, with the original 0.0005 head L2. Periodic coefficients have across-sensor standard deviations 0.55-0.82 traffic units, versus 1.2-1.8 for intercept/horizon, and neighbor periodic difference RMS about 0.53. Directional agreement gates are being compared on identical cached OOF experts before choosing the next public candidate.\n\nDirectional agreement gate rejected locally: unheaded **13.4517430 / 13.2056779**, trend **13.4519279 / 13.2004239**, graph **13.4353476 / 13.1899886**. Each worsens both blocks relative to its matching seven-variable gate. No protected evaluation was used for this rejection. The graph-head/standard-gate candidate is now submitted through `./solve.sh`; compare only its actual complete protected result against the best 14.018026311821254.\n\nGraph-head complete public evaluation **passed and improved**: MAE **14.007650660881973**, score **2.9877325587049133**, evaluation `f97eaab0c1764a1095465feadf1ed8ef`, unchanged seeds 17/29/43, all quality gates passed. Improvement over previous best is **0.010375650939281**. Retained graph head and matching standard gate in `method.py`. Next local test uses four horizon-by-uncertainty interactions in the gate, comparing the identical cached OOF experts with no additional backbone fits.\n\nHorizon-interaction gate local MAE (last / middle): unheaded **13.4462557 / 13.1903042**, trend **13.4444031 / 13.1858166**, graph **13.4303059 / 13.1785834**. Each improves both blocks over its matching standard gate. The four new terms multiply centered horizon by relative anchor/base disagreement, recent/base disagreement, history variability and expert disagreement; retain the original 0.01 gate penalty and clipping. Submitted graph-head + interaction-gate candidate for complete protected scoring, with graph-head/standard-gate MAE 14.007650660881973 saved as fallback.\n{\n  \"policy_name\": \"graph_shared_seasonal_conditional_blend\",\n  \"method_summary\": \"Adds sensor intercept, horizon and Fourier heads to the residual network, with a learned-neighborhood Laplacian penalty sharing only the four seasonal coefficients, then refits the gate from matching origin cross-fits. Complete protected masked MAE improves from 14.0180263118 to 14.0076506609 under unchanged seeds 17, 29 and 43, with all quality gates passing; the graph-head method is retained.\"\n}\n\"\"\"Graph-shared seasonal experts with a horizon-interaction residual gate.\"\"\"\nimport conditional_calibration\n\n\ndef fit(features, targets, seed):\n    return conditional_calibration.fit(features, targets, seed, site_head='graph',\n                                       gate_mode='interactions')\n\n\ndef predict(state, features):\n    return conditional_calibration.predict(state, features)\n#!/bin/sh\nset -eu\npython /opt/forecast-engine/evaluate.py --solution /workspace/solution\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
